      "id": "def-orthogonal-clifford-families-and-centrioles",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "math81_sugawara_completion",
      "reason": "The current complete source supports this not-applicable disposition for the actual candidate: The trace factor1/p requires positive even p and each P_j is the component containing the supplied J_j; the Definition makes no assertion for a component with no selected member."
    },
    {
      "id": "def-vertex-algebra-state-field",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "math81_sugawara_completion",
      "reason": "The Definition requires a nonzero vacuum1, so V cannot be zero or have empty carrier. The displayed coefficient families have fixed index sets Z (field modes) and nonnegative integers (creation powers), neither empty. An individual state may have a zero field, but that is a zero-valued indexed family, not an empty family; creation at the vacuum retains the identity mode. Thus the sum syntax does not create a separate empty-index assertion."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-affine-current-fields-are-local",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "math81_sugawara_completion",
      "reason": "The input vacuum module and its vacuum are fixed; the current and delta sums run over all integers, and the creation sum over r>=0. Proof1.1 uses restrictedness for truncation on each vector, while2.1 explicitly treats the reindexings coefficientwise with finite sums. Even when x=0 or [x,y]=0, the same integer-indexed families have zero coefficients; the proof asserts no result about an empty current-index family."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-symmetric-gaussian-alternating-sum-vanishes",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "final_coverage_source_reconciliation",
      "reason": "Proof step 1.1 has m+1 summands and m factors; m≥1 makes both index sets nonempty. Proof step 2.1 chooses j=(m−1−d)/2 inside that nonempty factor set by the actual parity and bounds. The diagnostic matches sum notation, but an empty aggregate cannot occur in this lemma; m=0 is excluded."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-algebraic-milnor-neighborhoods-admit-controlled-sector-transport",
      "case": "empty",
      "by": "/root/math81_frattini_placement",
      "reason": "The construction supplies cofinal pointed Milnor tubes, transverse sphere boundaries and controlled transport; it does not characterize every possible neighborhood. The input fixes p in f inverse of zero. Its neighborhoods all contain p, and the cofinal family constructed by choosing a center and radius is nonempty; an empty pointed space is excluded."
    },
    {
